    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: #92400e;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .chart-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .rec-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .two-col { columns: 1; }
    header h1 { font-size: 1.4rem; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
  <h1>BIEK Computer Science 12th Class (HSC Part-2)<br>Past Paper Trend Analysis</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">11-Year Longitudinal Study: 2015 – 2025 | Question Type, Volume &amp; Topic Patterns</div>
  <div class="badge-row">
    <span class="badge">327 Questions</span>
    <span class="badge">10 Years</span>
    <span class="badge">3 Question Types</span>
    <span class="badge">BIEK HSC Part-2</span>
  </div>
</header>

<nav>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="#overview" class="active">Overview</a></li>
    <li><a href="#yearly">Year-by-Year</a></li>
    <li><a href="#types">Question Types</a></li>
    <li><a href="#topics">Topic Patterns</a></li>
    <li><a href="#insights">Exam Prep Insights</a></li>
    <li><a href="#conclusions">Conclusions</a></li>
  </ul>
</nav>

<div class="container">

<!-- ======================= SECTION 1: OVERVIEW ======================= -->
<section id="overview">
  <div class="section-label">Section 1</div>
  <h2>Dataset &amp; Examination Overview</h2>

  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value">327</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Total Questions</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Across all 10 years</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value">2015–2025</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Year Range</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">10 of 11 years present</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value">45.9%</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">MCQ Share</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">150 of 327 questions</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value">3</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Question Types</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">MCQs · Short · Long</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="missing-note">
    <strong>Data Integrity Note:</strong> Examination year 2020 is absent from the dataset. The BIEK 2020 examinations were likely not held or not compiled due to COVID-19 disruptions. This gap must be considered when interpreting period-level trends. The analysis below reflects only the 10 available years.
  </div>

  <h3>Question Type Summary</h3>
  <div class="bar-row">
    <div class="bar-label">MCQs</div>
    <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill mcq" id="bar-mcq"></div></div>
    <div class="bar-val">150 <span style="font-weight:400;color:var(--text-muted)">(45.9%)</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="bar-row">
    <div class="bar-label">Short Qs</div>
    <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill short" id="bar-short"></div></div>
    <div class="bar-val">147 <span style="font-weight:400;color:var(--text-muted)">(45.0%)</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="bar-row">
    <div class="bar-label">Long Qs</div>
    <div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill long" id="bar-long"></div></div>
    <div class="bar-val">30 <span style="font-weight:400;color:var(--text-muted)">(9.2%)</span></div>
  </div>

  <h3>Average Questions Per Year (by Type)</h3>
  <div class="chart-row">
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h4>Average by Type</h4>
      <div class="chart-wrap short-h">
        <canvas id="avgTypeChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h4>Type Share Pie</h4>
      <div class="chart-wrap short-h">
        <canvas id="pieChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="callout blue">
    <div class="callout-title">Key Structural Finding</div>
    The exam has three stable structural anchors: <strong>exactly 15 MCQs per year</strong> (the single most consistent number across the entire dataset), <strong>exactly 3 Long Questions per year</strong>, and a Short Question count that shifted from 9 → 18 → 15 across distinct periods. These three anchors reflect the official BIEK paper blueprint.
  </div>
</section>


<!-- ======================= SECTION 2: YEAR-BY-YEAR ======================= -->
<section id="yearly">
  <div class="section-label">Section 2</div>
  <h2>Year-by-Year Question Volume Analysis</h2>

  <div class="chart-row full">
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h4>Total Questions per Year</h4>
      <div class="chart-wrap tall">
        <canvas id="totalBarChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>Year-by-Year Breakdown Table</h3>
  <table id="yoyTable">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Year</th>
        <th class="num">MCQs</th>
        <th class="num">Short</th>
        <th class="num">Long</th>
        <th class="num">Total</th>
        <th class="num">YoY Change</th>
        <th class="num">MCQ %</th>
        <th class="num">Short %</th>
        <th class="num">Long %</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody></tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="chart-row full">
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h4>Year-over-Year Total Change</h4>
      <div class="chart-wrap tall">
        <canvas id="yoyChangeChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <div class="callout-title">Volume Pattern — Three Distinct Periods</div>
    The data reveals <strong>three structurally distinct periods</strong> rather than a single stable exam:
    <br><strong>Period A (2015–2016):</strong> 27 questions total — 15 MCQ, 9 Short, 3 Long.
    <br><strong>Period B (2017–2019):</strong> 36 questions total — 15 MCQ, 18 Short, 3 Long. A sudden +9 question expansion.
    <br><strong>Period C (2021–2025):</strong> 33 questions total — 15 MCQ, 15 Short, 3 Long. A post-COVID contraction of Short questions from 18 to 15.
  </div>
</section>


<!-- ======================= SECTION 3: QUESTION TYPE ANALYSIS ======================= -->
<section id="types">
  <div class="section-label">Section 3</div>
  <h2>Question Type Composition &amp; Trends</h2>

  <div class="chart-row full">
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h4>Stacked: MCQ, Short &amp; Long Questions by Year</h4>
      <div class="chart-wrap tall">
        <canvas id="stackedChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-row">
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h4>MCQ Count Over Time</h4>
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <canvas id="mcqLineChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h4>Short Q Count Over Time</h4>
      <div class="chart-wrap">
        <canvas id="shortLineChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-row full">
    <div class="chart-card">
      <h4>Type Proportion Stacked Area (%)</h4>
      <div class="chart-wrap tall">
        <canvas id="areaChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>Long Questions — Per-Year Consistency</h3>
  <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-muted);margin-bottom:1rem;">
    Long Questions show the strongest stability in the entire dataset: exactly 3 per year across all 10 years, yielding a standard deviation of 0. This translates to a consistent 8.3%–11.1% share depending on the period. No other question type matches this level of year-over-year invariance.
  </p>

  <h3>Type Ratio Summary</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Period</th>
        <th class="num">Years</th>
        <th class="num">Avg MCQ %</th>
        <th class="num">Avg Short %</th>
        <th class="num">Avg Long %</th>
        <th>Character</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
