  <h2>Strategic Insights for Exam Preparation</h2>

  <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-muted);margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
    The following recommendations are derived directly from the 11-year pattern data. Each is tied to a specific statistical finding from the dataset.
  </p>

  <div class="rec-grid">
    <div class="rec-card high">
      <h4><span class="rec-num">1</span>Master Loop-Based Control Structures</h4>
      <p>Control Structures (244 mentions) are the single most frequently tested topic. The for loop, while loop, do-while loop, nested loops, break and continue statements appear in MCQs, Short, and Long questions across <em>every year</em> without exception. Expect at least 2–4 questions on this topic per paper.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card high">
      <h4><span class="rec-num">2</span>Build Strong Database Foundations</h4>
      <p>Database Concepts (226 mentions) rival Control Structures in frequency. Candidates must command primary key, foreign key, candidate key, relationships (one-to-one, one-to-many, many-to-many), DBMS advantages, and RDBMS features. These appear in both MCQs and Short/Long questions.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card high">
      <h4><span class="rec-num">3</span>Never Skip C Fundamentals</h4>
      <p>C Programming Fundamentals (172 mentions) and Data Types &amp; Variables (174 mentions) together form the third pillar. Keywords like <em>variable</em>, <em>operator</em>, <em>format specifier</em>, <em>int</em>, <em>float</em>, <em>printf</em>, and <em>identifier</em> appear persistently in MCQ form. Short questions frequently ask for printf() output or operator differences.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card high">
      <h4><span class="rec-num">4</span>Prepare for Fixed Long Question Slots</h4>
      <p>There are always exactly 3 Long Questions per paper. Past patterns show Long Q3 typically covers Control Structures or Functions; Long Q4 covers Operators or Data Types or File Handling; Long Q5 covers Database Concepts or MS Access Objects. Use this as a structural guide for topic revision sequencing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rec-card">
      <h4><span class="rec-num">5</span>Watch the Shift in Short Question Count</h4>
      <p>Since 2021, Short Questions have been set at 15 (down from 18 in 2017–2019). This period-C structure appears stable. Students should aim to answer 12–14 Short Questions competently rather than relying on the older 18-question preparation strategy.</p>
